## Observed pair

| Metric | A2 | B2 |
|---|---:|---:|
| Acceptance/profile | counted / stage4a | counted / stage4a |
| Retired / budget | 2,999,999,998 / 3,000,000,000 | 2,999,999,998 / 3,000,000,000 |
| Delivered #PF / #GP(0) | 33 / 1 | 33 / 1 |
| IRQ0 edges / delivered IRQs | 34,799 / 34,804 | 34,801 / 34,806 |
| RDTSC reads | 34,438,590 | 34,440,100 |
| Quanta | 34,564,457 | 34,566,115 |
| Virtual ns | 37,456,987,535 | 37,458,683,038 |
| PIT counter reads / PM timer reads | 16,672 / 230 | 16,672 / 230 |
| Selected ordinal status | 30 / captured | 30 / captured |

For ordinal 30, both sidecars report a CPL3 instruction-fetch #PF at RIP=CR2 `0x4000b0`, error code `0x00000014`, with original fault walk `NotPresent { level: Pml4 }` and raw PML4 entry value `0x0`. The matching post-IRET context restores CPL3, CS `0x0033`, RIP `0x4000b0`, and the same run's user RSP. In each run the CR3 is unchanged from the fault context. The post-IRET walk is translated in both runs to physical `0x443d0b0`; its final PT entry is index 0, value `0x443d025`. Intermediate paging-structure addresses and user RSP differ between runs because the runtime layout differs; the final mapping is identical.

The pair observes that the selected mapping is absent at the original fetch and present at the matching IRET return boundary. It does not prove that the retried fetch retired or that the guest TLB has any particular state.

Counters differ by 2 IRQ0 edges/deliveries, 1,510 RDTSC reads, 1,658 quanta, and 1,695,503 virtual ns. These timing/scheduling differences are not normalized and are not classified benign. This was not a strict automatic series comparison. Earlier event-presence variation and timing variation (including `delay_tsc+0x4d`) remain open; S5-07 remains blocked/unaccepted.

